<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Coverage settings for the collector run documented in
  .claude/skills/startup/references/testing.md (pass this file with the `settings` option of
  `dotnet test`, alongside `collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"`).

  The point of the exclusions is to make the number mean something. ClaudeMon is a WinForms tray
  app, so a large slice of it is desktop-bound: Forms, Controls, NativeWindow hosts, Win32/registry
  interop and the process entry points. None of that can run in a headless test host, so leaving it
  in produces a headline percentage that is dominated by code nobody can ever cover — and a
  regression in the logic layer disappears into the noise.

  What is left after the exclusions is the "logic layer" the CI gate protects: Configuration,
  Models, Monitoring, Services, plus the pure UI helpers that were deliberately extracted out of
  the forms so they *are* testable (the *Layout / *Metrics / *Placement / *Text classes,
  IconRenderer, Sparkline, Theme, DpiScale, ForegroundMonitor).

  Rule of thumb when adding a class here: exclude it only if it genuinely cannot run without a
  live Windows desktop or a message loop. "It has no tests yet" is not a reason — that is exactly
  what the gate is meant to notice.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat code coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <Exclude>
            [ClaudeMon]ApplicationConfiguration,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.Program,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.TrayApplication,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.Services.SystemSessionEvents,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.AboutDialog,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.FlyoutPanel,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.SettingsForm,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.SystemTheme,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TabStrip,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TabStrip/*,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TaskbarEnumerator,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TaskbarInfo,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TaskbarOverlayManager,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TaskbarOverlayManager/*,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.TaskbarOverlayWindow,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.ThemedNumericUpDown,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.ToggleSwitch,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.UpdateAvailableDialog,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.UpdateDownloadDialog,
            [ClaudeMon]ClaudeMon.UI.UsageBreakdownForm
          </Exclude>
          <!-- ExcludeByAttribute is deliberately left at coverlet's default. Adding
               CompilerGeneratedAttribute here also drops record members and async state machines,
               which shifts per-class numbers in both directions and makes the gate hard to reason
               about; keeping the default means the gate number is just "the usual coverlet number,
               minus the desktop-bound classes above". -->
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
